35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Mizuki, the yard devices are a mess, and that 2021 trial failed fast. We need a system that fits our actual calendar, not just a demo.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Kenji, the invoices confirm it. Bundled prices held steady, but separate add-ons climbed yearly. We are buying a leaky bucket.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mizuki, that leaky bucket is exactly why I checked the outage. Support was unowned for two days. We are walking into the same trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Asuka, the 2018 data lift was a disaster. Mismatched codes lasted a year. We can’t trust outside teams to fix our mess.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Rin, the people side is just as fragile. Two key administrators retire this year, and the last hiring took eleven months. We are thin.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, that staffing gap scares me. If we pick a system needing constant hands-on help, we are doomed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Kenji, exactly. The board minutes show capital gets cut, but operating costs pass easily. We are funding the leak, not the fix.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mizuki, the warehouse rules were rewritten twice in one year. The plan we sign today will be obsolete before the ink dries.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Asuka, and the dispatch tool skipped three upgrades because testing took too long. It just aged in place. We can’t repeat that.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Rin, the supervisors dropped the new routines within weeks. If we don’t respect their existing habits, the system will fail before it starts.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, that confirms it. We need a vendor who stays on-site to keep the yard running, not just a remote support line.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Kenji, on-site presence is expensive. I need to know if that cost is a one-time capital hit or a recurring operating line.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, if it’s recurring, we’re stuck. I need a single owner for support, not four suppliers pointing fingers like last winter.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
